<pdd-reason>Provide an immediately usable Ubuntu application launcher and user-local executable.</pdd-reason>
<pdd-dependency>build_bash.prompt</pdd-dependency>
Implement install.sh with bash strict mode. Build release, copy executable to a temporary file in ~/.local/lib/personal-files then atomically rename to personal-files, allowing upgrade while the previous binary is running. Install the SVG into XDG_DATA_HOME/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps and the bundled PNG sizes 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 128, 256 and 512 into the matching hicolor apps directories. Create XDG_DATA_HOME/applications/io.monoclaw.PersonalFiles.desktop named Personal Files with quoted Exec plus %f, Terminal=false and file-manager categories. Set Icon to the absolute installed 512 PNG so a running shell does not fall back to the generic executable glyph. Escape Desktop Entry Exec special characters and percent placeholders; never shell-evaluate paths. Add ~/.local/bin/personal-files symlink, preserving an existing non-symlink. Update desktop database when available. Do not register as the default file manager or require sudo. Installed binary must run independently of the repository or /tmp.
